-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Texas Instruments LMX9838 SimplyBlue Bluetooth module
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These are example captures of the UART command interface of an LMX9838
"SimplyBlue" Bluetooth serial port module (AN-1699 command set), taken
between a host PC running the Simply Blue Commander tool and the module
inside a DiaLink J2534 automotive diagnostic adapter.

The module runs at 921600 baud, 8n1.

Details:
https://www.ti.com/product/LMX9838
https://www.ti.com/lit/an/snoa498b/snoa498b.pdf (AN-1699 Software User's Guide)


Logic analyzer setup
--------------------

The logic analyzer used was a Chip&Dip RDC2-0064 (at 4MHz):

  Probe    LMX9838
  -----------------
  0 (TX)   TX (module -> host)
  1 (RX)   RX (host -> module)


lmx9838_gap_read_local_name.sr
------------------------------

Host reads the friendly name of the module:

  RX: 02 52 03 00 00 55 03                  REQ GAP_READ_LOCAL_NAME
  TX: 02 43 03 14 00 5A 00 12 "DiaLink #D1625359" 00 03
                                            CFM GAP_READ_LOCAL_NAME,
                                            Status: OK


lmx9838_gap_read_local_bda.sr
-----------------------------

Host reads the Bluetooth address of the module; the module's firmware
refuses the command:

  RX: 02 52 05 00 00 57 03                  REQ GAP_READ_LOCAL_BDA
  TX: 02 43 05 01 00 49 32 03               CFM GAP_READ_LOCAL_BDA,
                                            Status: ERROR_COMMAND_DISALLOWED
